 Sequence role: On the active route AirMusic follows Effect Sound, where one oscillation changed another's phase; here a brief contact starts a decaying oscillation, and two of them can sound together. The additive sum in the Synthesis Lab is where this leads: every note here is one sinusoid under one decay, and the ribbon above the bars already draws their sum. The hall keeps its wider company — the looper, the drone, the pipes — as the ambient layer round a walkable void.
 
-Technical angle: `resonating_metallophone` (`algorithms/wavefunctions/resonance/`): a row of `ResonatingBar` rigid bodies, each with its own `AudioStreamPlayer3D` and a note it renders once — `sin(2π·f·t) · exp(−t / decay_time)`, decay 3 s, 7.5 s long, eased to silence — so voices on different bars overlap and a re-struck bar starts again. Bar length follows `BAR_LENGTH · sqrt(root / f)`, the free-bar relation, so the scale is visible. The striker is an XR Tools pickable rod; a held pickable is frozen, kinematic, moved to a pick-up collision layer with its mask cleared, and the bars now listen on that layer so a strike in hand forms a contact and `body_entered` rings the bar; the striker's speed, measured per physics frame by the instrument, sets the strike's strength. Under `#stand:table` the row sits on a table at 0.85 m, the bars locked in place and kept awake, the striker in a cradle at the left end it returns to after three seconds elsewhere, the Hz labels and the instruction on the table's front, a 12 ms scope of the bars' own generated samples and a voices/age readout above the row. The tuning axis (`#tuning:pentatonic|equal|just|harmonic`) re-cuts the row; the shipped pentatonic is what this hall offers.
+Technical angle: `resonating_metallophone` (`algorithms/wavefunctions/resonance/`): a row of `ResonatingBar` rigid bodies, each with its own `AudioStreamPlayer3D` and a note it renders once — `sin(2π·f·t) · exp(−t / decay_time)`, decay 3 s, 7.5 s long, eased to silence — so voices on different bars overlap and a re-struck bar starts again. Bar length follows `BAR_LENGTH · sqrt(root / f)`, the free-bar relation, so the scale is visible. The striker is an XR Tools pickable rod; a held pickable is frozen, kinematic, moved to a pick-up collision layer with its mask cleared, and a `StrikeZone` area detects the held tip while the rigid contact signal remains available for a thrown or dropped striker; the striker's speed, measured per physics frame by the instrument, sets the strike's strength. Under `#stand:table` the row sits on a table at 0.85 m, the bars locked in place and kept awake, the striker in a cradle at the left end it returns to after three seconds elsewhere, the Hz labels and the instruction on the table's front, a 12 ms scope of the bars' own generated samples and a voices/age readout above the row. The tuning axis (`#tuning:pentatonic|equal|just|harmonic`) re-cuts the row; the shipped pentatonic is what this hall offers.
 
 Critical angle: The instrument synthesises a resonance; it does not solve a metal bar. That is a decision the room states rather than hides, and it leaves the visible relation between length and pitch intact. The pentatonic cut decides which pairs of notes a visitor can put together; another cut would offer other pairs. The readout that names each voice's age is the room's way of separating the strike from what the strike began, which is the distinction the next rooms depend on.
 
